{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": "Reviewed evidence for the Reach record. A Reach record says where a Binding can be reached; it references a binding digest and never enters Binding identity, so moving a deployment reissues the record and changes nothing that was pinned. Holding a record is not authority: the caller still binds atomically against the manifest it fetches and the host still admits every call. Digests are computed over boundary.reach/v1 with canonical JSON, excluding the reserved signature field. A gate may verify these vectors but must never rewrite them.",
  "domain": "boundary.reach/v1",
  "signatureReserved": true,
  "$signatureNote": "Version 1 records are unsigned. The field is reserved so adding a signature later does not change the record shape, and it is excluded from the digest because a signature signs a digest and cannot be part of what it signs.",
